What is Cartilage Regeneration Technology?

Cartilage regeneration technologies represent cutting-edge medical solutions designed to repair or replace damaged articular cartilage, primarily used in orthopedic treatments for joints like knees and ankles. These advanced approaches include autologous chondrocyte implantation (ACI), stem cell therapies, and tissue engineering techniques that stimulate the body's natural healing mechanisms. Unlike traditional joint replacement surgeries, these regeneration methods preserve natural joint anatomy while restoring functionality.

